  {
    "sha": "6aa630feec8eebb98be69e4ed0f5e3fd7fc7e84d",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVVonwNoAKDZhYTYzMGZlZWM4ZWViYjk4YmU2OWU0ZWQwZjVlM2ZkN2ZjN2U4NGQ",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T03:00:45Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "NeoTech",
        "email": "168627+NeoTech@users.noreply.github.com",
        "date": "2026-11-27T03:00:45Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(pathkernel): later stages rebuild a curve through its family\n\nThe K4 order stage reversed a curve with Curve::new, which refuses the\nhelix family: a valid helix guide set was refused with the constructor's\nreason HELIX_NEEDS_LEAD (review of PR #4244 at 33c116cfa).\n\nOne rule for the class: a later stage that restarts, reverses or\nreplaces a curve makes it again through the constructor of the curve's\nfamily (Curve::with_points: Curve::helix with the same circle and lead,\nelse Curve::new with the same circle), or refuses by its own reason.\n\n- Order: a helix always runs down its lead (reversed only when the guide\n  set holds it upward); a direction that its hand does not give is named\n  by the note HELIX_HAND_SETS_DIRECTION. A failed rebuild is the order\n  reason NOT_REVERSIBLE.\n- Load: constant engagement inserts passes only before a ring\n  (NOT_A_RING else); trochoidal loops leave a curve with a lead, an exact\n  circle or a changing depth as it is (SHAPE_KEPT); a refused rebuild is\n  SET_NOT_KEPT, loops that make no curve LOOPS_NOT_A_CURVE.\n- Table test later_stages: each guide family against each later stage;\n  the trace chain-region table gets the load stage rows.\n- Doc sentence of segment_gap made clear.\n\nRefs #4176\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
